<http://ontology.ipbes.net/report/il/TCA24-Table1.1> a ipbes:Illustration ;
    dcterms:identifier "Table1.1" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Five broad categories of the roles that people play in the process of transformative change." .

<http://ontology.ipbes.net/report/il/TCA24-Table1.2> a ipbes:Illustration ;
    dcterms:identifier "Table1.2" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Types of actions for transformative change for a just and sustainable world." .

<http://ontology.ipbes.net/report/il/TCA24-Table1.3> a ipbes:Illustration ;
    ipbes:hasDescription "The analyses of the transformative change assessment corpus of literature on case studies (referred to hereafter as case corpus) used 17 actor groups as described in the second column." ;
    dcterms:identifier "Table1.3" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Summary of actor types and actor groups, exemplified with initiatives from the case study database." .

<http://ontology.ipbes.net/report/il/TCA24-Table1.4> a ipbes:Illustration ;
    dcterms:identifier "Table1.4" ;
    skos:prefLabel "The typology of knowledge gaps identified as relevant and used in this assessment." .

<http://ontology.ipbes.net/report/il/TCA24-Table2.1> a ipbes:Illustration ;
    dcterms:identifier "Table2.1" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Five highlighted alternative economic visions." .

<http://ontology.ipbes.net/report/il/TCA24-Table2.2> a ipbes:Illustration ;
    ipbes:hasDescription "Endpoints here are considered as collective ‘placements’ (mapping) of visions within the Nature Futures Framework according to how nature is valued and are based on the original six endpoints of Durán et al. (2023) and connected to the clusters of visions. Specific pathways to endpoints are examined more closely in Annex 2.3." ;
    dcterms:identifier "Table2.2" ;
