<http://ontology.ipbes.net/report/sch/TCA24-2.3.5> a ipbes:SubChapter ;
    ipbes:Chapter <http://ontology.ipbes.net/report/ch/TCA24ch2> ;
    ipbes:KeyMessage <http://ontology.ipbes.net/report/key/TCA24-KM3>,
        <http://ontology.ipbes.net/report/key/TCA24-KM6> ;
    ipbes:Reference <http://ontology.ipbes.net/report/ref/4589462/items/464MH6QA>,
        <http://ontology.ipbes.net/report/ref/4589462/items/6IKHJLFH>,
        <http://ontology.ipbes.net/report/ref/4589462/items/EP4D5V6L>,
        <http://ontology.ipbes.net/report/ref/4589462/items/FCLT5HTW>,
        <http://ontology.ipbes.net/report/ref/4589462/items/V5WX3GPE> ;
    ipbes:Report ipbes:TCA24 ;
    ipbes:SubChapter <http://ontology.ipbes.net/report/sch/TCA24-2.3> ;
    ipbes:hasDescription """This subsection analyses 17 illustrative examples from the case study database that showcase transformative potential. These examples are developed by different groups of actors which engage with diverse views, structures and practices, aiming to address the four principles of transformative change indicated in Chapter 1. The visions behind these cases are designed to inspire transformative change to address biodiversity loss and nature’s decline.

To assess the potential of visions to bring about transformative change, a joint analysis of the visions was conducted with evidence in the vision database from Chapter 2 (n=881) and the transformative change assessment case study database (referred to hereafter as the case study database) (n=391). The analysis indicated that cases of transformative change that include explicit or implicit visions have more positive outcomes in ecological, economic and social dimensions (Figure 2.7-A). In addition, cases that included actions by Indigenous Peoples had a greater likelihood of transformative change compared to cases that did not (Figure 2.7-B). Finally, visions developed with higher levels of participation addressed more comprehensive sets of purposes for nature and people and more drivers of change (Figure 2.7-C).

Notes
16. Case study database with transformative potential and pitfalls (https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.10260233).""" ;
    dcterms:identifier "2.3.5" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Realizing transformative changes through visions" .

